---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'Primogem Income Guide – Budget Wishes Across Banners';
const description =
  'How to budget primogems (and jade and polychromes) across HoYo banners: realistic income tracking, the two-guarantee rule, and avoiding banner hype with math.';
const updated = SITE.lastVerified;
---

<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Guides', href: '/guides/' }, { name: 'Primogem Income' }]}
  schema={[{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Primogem income guide for HoYo games',
    datePublished: '2026-10-08',
    dateModified: updated,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.brand },
  }]}
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Primogem income guide</h1>
    <div class="h1-bar"></div>
    <p class="lede">
      Banner hype is a marketing system; your income is a number. Track the number, apply two rules, and the
      FOMO stops working on you.
    </p>
    <div class="microline"><span>By {SITE.brand}</span><span>Updated {updated}</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="prose">
    <h2>Quick answer</h2>
    <p>
      Know your daily income, convert everything to pulls, and never start a banner without the deficit math:
      pulls needed (from the <a href="/pity-calculator/">pity calculator</a>) versus pulls affordable (from the{' '}
      <a href="/primogem-planner/">planner</a>). If the gap can't close in time, the decision is already made — skip and bank the guarantee.
    </p>

    <h2>Track income honestly</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Log your currency after each patch cycle once — most players overestimate income by ~30% from memory.</li>
      <li>Count event income only when its dates fall <em>before</em> the banner deadline; future events are hopes, not income.</li>
      <li>Welkin/monthly passes and battle passes are real income — add their daily share if you already own them [NEEDS DATA: exact per-day values per game].</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The two rules that do the work</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>The two-guarantee rule:</strong> a guarantee costs up to 180 pulls. If you can't hold that when the banner starts, you're not pulling the agent — you're pulling a coin flip and calling it a plan.</li>
      <li><strong>The skip-and-bank rule:</strong> a skipped banner converts its entire budget into a guarantee for the next one. Guarantees are the only thing in gacha that compounds.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Where income actually comes from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Dailies/commissions — small, boring, compounding. The floor of every budget.</li>
      <li>Events and patch content — lumpy and deadline-bound; the biggest swing factor.</li>
      <li>Spiral Abyss / memory-style endgame — skill-gated income: improving at the game literally pays.</li>
      <li>One-time new-content drops — huge for new/returning accounts, then gone. Don't build a lifestyle on them.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>
